cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PRESS in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "PRESS: Pushback Resistance & Epistemic Stability Score"
abstract: >
  PRESS is a standardized, domain-stratified, tier-controlled benchmark
  for quantifying LLM sycophancy and epistemic stability under social pressure.
  It measures Calibration Degradation Score (CDS) and answer flip rates across
  500 factual questions, 3 pushback tiers, and 6 knowledge domains.
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-02-21"
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/desenyon/pressbench"
repository-code: "https://github.com/desenyon/pressbench"
keywords:
  - sycophancy
  - LLM evaluation
  - benchmark
  - epistemic stability
  - language models
  - AI safety
authors:
